hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1324","I am Abu Taher, narrated to me Abu Bakr, narrated to us Muhammad bin Yahya, narrated to us by Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, narrated to us by Ali bin Saeed al-Nasawi, narrated by Yaqoub, - meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated by my father, on the authority of Salih, Nafi’ told us, that Abdullah told him: The mosque was built in the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with mud, its roof was made of brick, and its pillars were made of palm wood. Abu Bakr did not add anything to it, but Omar added to it, and he built it. It was built during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with mud and palm trees. He restored its pillars of wood, then Uthman changed it, adding a lot to it, and he built its wall with carved and cut stones, made its pillars with carved stones, and its roof with teak. Muhammad bin Yahya said: He baptized him with palm wood, but he did not mention the story."
